            e\n   223\t                          (throw (refuse (path dir)\n   224\t                                         (str \"it cannot be read (\"\n   225\t                                              (or (ex-message e) (str e))\n   226\t                                              \")\")))))]\n   227\t    (text->config (path dir) text)))\n   228\t\n   229\t\n   230\t(defn- mkdirs!\n   231\t  [dir]\n   232\t  #?(:cljd (.createSync (dart-io/Directory. dir) .recursive true)\n   233\t     :clj (.mkdirs (java.io.File. ^String dir))\n   234\t     :cljs (.mkdirSync (js/require \"fs\") dir #js {:recursive true})))\n   235\t\n   236\t\n   237\t(defn- render\n   238\t  \"The state file's text, one setting to a line, with no space before a\n   239\t   closing bracket (ClojureDart's EDN reader refuses one).\"\n   240\t  [flags]\n   241\t  (let [entries (for [[flag _] saved-flags\n   242\t                      :let [v (get flags flag)]\n   243\t                      :when (some? v)]\n   244\t                  (str (config-key flag) \" \" (pr-str v)))]\n   245\t    (str \"{:version \" version \"\\n :config {\"\n   246\t         (str/join \"\\n          \" entries)\n   247\t         \"}}\\n\")))\n   248\t\n   249\t\n   250\t(defn save!\n   251\t  \"Write `flags` as the state file of the node directory `dir`, creating the\n   252\t   directory and replacing any earlier file atomically.\"\n   253\t  [dir flags]\n   254\t  (mkdirs! dir)\n   255\t  (fs/atomic-replace! dir file-name (render flags)))\n    80\t- **Changing it:** a flag overrides the saved value for that setting, and the\n    81\t  result is saved. A repeated flag (`--dht-peer`, `--dht-principal`)\n    82\t  replaces all of its saved values rather than adding to them. `dht init`\n    83\t  saves publishing; `dht serve` and `dht join` clear it. A bare switch\n    84\t  (`--headless`, `--dht-publish`) cannot be turned off by a flag, so use\n    85\t  `--reset`.\n    86\t- **`--reset`** forgets the saved state and starts from the command line\n    87\t  alone; the result is saved. **`--no-state`** neither reads nor writes it,\n    88\t  for a one-off run.\n    89\t- **Refusals:** a state file that cannot be read, or saved flags that clash\n    90\t  with the command line (saved `--dht-*` flags with `--index-store mem`), refuse\n    91\t  startup, naming the file and `--reset`. A state file that cannot be written\n    92\t  is a warning, and the node still starts.\n    93\t- **Hosts:** ClojureDart has no home directory, so a bare `yin-repl` there\n    94\t  saves nothing unless `--dir` names the node directory.\n    95\t- **One node per name:** the state file is only as protected as its\n    96\t  directory. `dht init|serve|join` put the store in the node directory, so the\n    97\t  store's lock also keeps one process per state file. A node whose store lives\n    98\t  elsewhere (`--index-store file:/tmp/a`, or the in-memory default) is not\n    99\t  covered: two such processes with the same `--name` or `--dir` overwrite each\n   100\t  other's file, last writer wins, and no process notices. Give each its own\n   101\t  node directory: a distinct `--name`, or a distinct `--dir` when you pass one.\n   102\t- **Values:** a flag's value that begins with `--` is taken as a missing\n   103\t  value and refused (`--dht-peer --dht-publish`), so a path that really\n   104\t  begins with `--` is written `./--name`.\n   105\t\n   106\t## Protocol and Architecture\n   107\t\n   108\t**`connect` returns immediately and reports its outcome when known.**\n   109\t`connect` composes the client boundary, attaches, and answers at once with\n   110\t`Attaching to …`; the driver prints `Connected to …` when the boundary\n   111\treports `/established`, and reports `/not-found` (an authoritative disclaimer,\n   112\tnot retried) or a reachability failure (which may succeed on retry) when that\n   113\tis what happened. No evaluation blocks on a promise, on any host.\n   114\t\n   115\t**`(vm :type)` offers four evaluators; the default is `:semantic`.**\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
